From d89a5fcfcad3ef9955afba537f0098f9e67366ca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 16:27:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(dsv41): recover headless DSML parameters, spacing
 variants, forced tool_choice, and preamble exits
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Extend the DeepSeek V4.1 structural DSML parser overlay while preserving
token-128825 provenance on unconstrained tool calling and the
VLLM_DSV41_STRUCTURAL_DSML=0 kill switch:
- Exit ParserState.TOOL_PREAMBLE on TOOL_END or non-whitespace plain text instead
  of dropping the remainder of the turn when <｜DSML｜ invoke> is absent.
- Accept 128825-gated DSML spacing/dialect variants (<｜DSML｜calls>,
  <｜DSML｜ call>, <｜DSML｜ tool_calls>, unspaced V4 <｜DSML｜tool_calls>,
  <｜DSML｜invoke name=", <｜DSML｜parameter, function_calls/function, optional
  whitespace before >, and closers) while keeping BPE-spelled markup as text.
- Close reasoning implicitly when a 128825-gated <｜DSML｜ invoke name=" appears
  directly inside <think> without </think> or <｜DSML｜ calls>.
- Buffer genuine-128825 headless <｜DSML｜ parameter ...> blocks outside
  TOOL_ARGS, recovering tool calls when declared request.tools schemas uniquely
  identify the target tool (including parameter-substituted-for-invoke headers,
  parallel headless calls, in-<think> headless calls, and EOS-truncated values)
  and quarantining ambiguous or undeclared blocks so raw DSML never leaks into
  assistant content.
- Under forced/named tool_choice, keep 128825 provenance enforced inside
  <think> while accepting post-</think> DSML markers spelled with ordinary
  tokens so string-based structural tags always extract as tool calls.

Upstream-base: 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354
Rationale: Achieves complete DSML recovery and quarantine across headless parameters, dialect variants, preamble exits, and xgrammar forced/named structural tags without relaxing unconstrained 128825 provenance.
Quality: Post-generation output parsing only; sampling-neutral and bit-identical on canonical replies and quoted-DSML string arguments.
Tests: pytest tests/parser/test_deepseek_v41_structural_closers.py tests/parser/engine/test_deepseek_v41_dsml_provenance.py tests/parser/engine/test_deepseek_v41.py tests/parser/engine/test_deepseek_v4.py tests/tool_parsers/test_deepseekv41_tool_parser.py (676 passed).
Upstream-status: Local DeepSeek-V4.1 structural DSML parser fix.
